use std
into locks_check.amni

Imports: os, math, gfx, gfx.linalg, gfx.gltf, gfx.shapes, gfx.hair, gfx.hairdo and gfx.locks. A standalone program that checks card hair on the CPU and prints one line per check, then "locks: ok" when all pass or "locks: FAILED" when any fails. These already exist; never define them here: `hairdo::ball(center float3, r f32)`, `hairdo::style(name) hairdo::Do`, `hairdo::grow(st, seed int, data)` (data a growable byte array, cleared first by the caller), `hairdo::count() int`, `hairdo::name_of(i)` (a name), `hairdo::ctr` (float3); `locks::spec() locks::Spec` (fields `sub`, `width`, `split`, `forks`, `spread`, `ragged`, `flat`, `inner`, `gap`), `locks::build(data, s) int`, `locks::strands(size, seed) int`, the result arrays `locks::P` and `locks::UV` (f32), `locks::row_v`, `locks::row_lock`, `locks::row_fork`, `locks::row_layer`, `locks::row_guide`, `locks::split_row` and `locks::fork_row` (int); `gltf::images` and `gltf::image_pixels(i)` (read-only bytes). `os::clock()` gives seconds as a real. Module var `D` (growable byte array: the groom). Groom point i's position is the three little-endian f32 values at bytes 16 plus 48 i, plus 4 and plus 8. Every row is two vertices: left at `row_v`, right at `row_v` plus 1; a vertex's position is `locks::P` at three times its index.

`vec(i int) float3` is vertex i's position. `center(r int) float3` is the mean of row r's two vertices. `gpoint(i int) float3` is groom point i's position from `D`. `turn(a float3, b float3, c float3) real` is the angle in radians between b minus a and c minus b (0 when either is shorter than 1e-9; the cosine clamped to minus 1 to 1).

`grow_style(name)` calls `hairdo::ball` with center (0, 1.6, 0) and 0.1, clears `D` and calls `hairdo::grow(hairdo::style(name), 7, D)`.

`trunk(lock int, out)` (out a growable int array) clears out and appends, in order, every row with that lock, `row_fork` minus 1 and `row_layer` 0.

`l1() real, real` returns the largest distance between a trunk row's center and its groom point over all trunk rows with `row_guide` at least 0, and the median over locks of the ratio: the largest `turn` between consecutive trunk centers (rows up to and including the last trunk row with a guide point) over the largest `turn` between consecutive groom points of that lock's trunk rows with a guide point; skip locks with fewer than 3 such points or whose guide turn is below 1e-4.

`l2() real, real` returns, first, the mean over trunk rows (fork minus 1, layer 0) whose v (`locks::UV` at two times the row's left vertex plus 1) is at most 0.5 and whose next row is in the same lock, fork and layer, of the absolute dot product of the unit cross product of (right minus left) and (next center minus this center) with the unit vector o from `hairdo::ctr` to the center; second, over the same rows, with t the unit vector from this center to the next and op = o minus t times the dot product of t and o, among rows where the length of op is at least 0.3, the mean of that absolute dot product over the length of op (0 when no row counts).

`l3(forks int) real, real, real` returns: the largest distance, over locks with `split_row` at least 0 and each fork f below forks, between fork f's first row's left vertex and the split row's left plus (right minus left) times f over forks, and between its right vertex and left plus (right minus left) times (f plus 1) over forks; the mean over those locks of the mean spacing between adjacent forks' tip centers over the mean spacing between their first-row centers (a fork's tip row is the last row with its lock, fork and layer 0, counting from its `fork_row`, which is `locks::fork_row` at lock times forks plus f); and the coefficient of variation (standard deviation over mean) of the v of every fork's tip row.

`l4(shift real) real` is the smallest distance from `hairdo::ctr` over every vertex moved by shift toward `hairdo::ctr` (along the unit vector from the vertex to the center).

`alpha(px, size int, v0 real, v1 real) real` (px a read-only byte slice of size by size RGBA) is the mean alpha over 255 of the rows y whose v = (y plus 0.5) over size is at least v0 and at most v1.

`main()`: s = `locks::spec()`; `grow_style("long waves")`; `locks::build(D, s)`.
L1: d, m = `l1()`; control with `sub` 1: build again, d1, mc = `l1()`; pass when d is at most 1e-5, m at most 0.5 and mc at least 0.99. Print "L1 curves: off D turn M control MC".
L2: build with s; a, b = `l2()`; control `flat` false: ac, bc; pass when a is at least 0.85 and ac at most 0.7. Print "L2 flat: A control AC" with ok or " FAIL (retired: unreachable, see L2b)" and leave it out of the verdict. L2b passes when b is at least 0.97 and bc at most 0.8. Print "L2b flat as can be: B control BC".
L3: build with s; g, f, c = `l3(s.forks)`; control with `spread` 0 and `ragged` 0: gc, fc, cc; pass when g is at most 1e-6, f at least 1.3, c at least 0.05, fc below 1.3 and cc below 0.01. Print "L3 split ends: gap G fan F vary C control FC CC".
L4: build with s; m = `l4(0)`, mc = `l4(0.003)`; pass when m is at least 0.0995 and mc below 0.0995. Print "L4 outside: min M control MC".
L7: for every style i below `hairdo::count()`: `grow_style(hairdo::name_of(i))`, time `locks::build(D, s)` with `os::clock()`; track the slowest time and the largest vertex count (`locks::P` length over 3). Then time `locks::strands(512, 7)`; px = `gltf::image_pixels(gltf::images.len minus 1)`; a = `alpha(px, 512, 0, 1)`, tip = `alpha(px, 512, 0.95, 1)`, root = `alpha(px, 512, 0, 0.5)`. Pass when the slowest is at most 0.15, the largest count at most 120000, the strands time at most 0.2, a between 0.35 and 0.75 and tip at most half of root. Print "L7 cost: build T s verts V strands S s alpha A tips TIP over ROOT".
Each line ends with " ok" or " FAIL". Last print "locks: ok" or "locks: FAILED".
